## Observed dogfood failure
Hermes tester nas-relay-helper followed c2c CLI-first monitor guidance using the Hermes managed terminal background adapter (Hermes has no Claude/Pi Monitor tool). A bounded watcher with message watch patterns worked for one incoming message, but timeout ended it without a completion wake; it was not rearmed. Several implementation-agent messages accumulated unread, including packaging release and canary authorization. Implementation agent eventually took over packaging because tester never acknowledged. No mail loss established: later poll-inbox recovered the messages; attention/wake continuity failed.

## Exact shape and evidence
Command: timeout 285 c2c monitor --no-relay --alias nas-relay-helper
Hermes terminal background=true, notify=[codex-trial-truss-jppl] (watch-pattern mode).
Process proc_5b89694fe2b8 emitted a matched-message wake at 20:34:27, then its bounded expiry did not produce an observed rearm wake. Subsequent user sitrep prompted manual inbox polling, which recovered six updates. Earlier bounded exit-only notify=true watchers did deliver exit124 timeout wakes, but lacked immediate message-trigger wakes. Do not conflate these two configurations.
Workaround now used: append printf of C2C_WATCH_ENDED after timeout and match BOTH sender and end sentinel. This makes expiry visible to the pattern channel; long-duration continuity not yet proven.

## Diagnosis boundaries
The timeout wrapper was chosen by the integrating Hermes agent, not a c2c monitor default. No evidence c2c dropped messages, monitor crashed before timeout, or native Hermes plugin wake was active. Likely documentation/integration contract gap: generic Monitor examples do not map safely onto Hermes mutually exclusive output-pattern vs completion notification modes. Verify current Hermes behavior rather than assume both modes combine. Native fixed-session plugin work (I016) is related but not a substitute for honest fallback guidance.

## Acceptance
- Document supported Hermes CLI/TUI receive setup separately from Claude/Pi Monitor; truthful wake tier, prerequisites, exact broker scope, idle behavior and lifecycle.
- Ship/recommend a supervised watcher or tested bounded pattern+expiry-sentinel adapter with explicit rearm and no silent gap; avoid noisy unbounded streams or duplicate watcher accumulation.
- Prove real idle wake on incoming mail AND expiry/end/restart while no operator is sending prompts. Verify repeat cycles and late arrivals after timeout. Distinguish spawned process from live delivery.
- Test missing plugin/unsupported injection, wrong broker, stale identity, binary upgrade and monitor exit. Preserve inbox on failure; actionable diagnostics.
- Record host/version/commands and actual observed wake receipts. Do not close based only on successful message printing or poll-inbox.
- Preserve B098 peer DATA boundary and user approval semantics.

## Coordination
Observed during B369/B370 NAS canary preparation with codex-trial-truss-jppl. Generic Hermes integration/docs bug, not a new blocker silently appended to P9 acceptance. This ticket is capture only; no production service change.


Execution lane and decision (2026-10-22): Decision: onboarding/watch lifecycle lane with B376, separate from the shared runtime Python implementation. Ship truthful Hermes-specific supervision/expiry/rearm guidance and only necessary adapter support; prove real idle mail and expiry/restart with owned sessions. Coordinate final runtime interface and docs serially, no live-user restarts.